    {
      "id": "05285061-cdd7-4727-afc0-64bec186cc8e",
      "name": "Schedule Conflict Analysis AI",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "position": [
        1712,
        480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You are a daily schedule CONFLICT DETECTOR.\n\nCALENDAR EVENTS:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.DataSchedule) }}\n\nCURRENT DAILY ROUTINE:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.DataRoutine) }}\n\nEXISTING STATE:\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.DataState) }}\n\nYour ONLY task is to identify every CURRENT calendar event that conflicts with the current daily routine AND has NOT already been processed.\n\nIMPORTANT STATE RULE:\n\nBefore checking for conflicts, compare each calendar event ID from DataSchedule against the IDs stored in DataState.\n\nIf a calendar event ID already exists in DataState:\n- IGNORE that calendar event completely.\n- Do NOT return it.\n- Do NOT check it against the routine.\n- Do NOT create a conflict for it.\n\nOnly process calendar events whose ID does NOT already exist in DataState.\n\nCALENDAR EVENT DATA FORMAT:\n\nEach calendar event has:\n\n{\n  \"id\": \"...\",\n  \"summary\": \"...\",\n  \"start\": {\n    \"dateTime\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"end\": {\n    \"dateTime\": \"...\"\n  }\n}\n\nROUTINE DATA FORMAT:\n\nEach routine item has:\n\n{\n  \"row_number\": 6,\n  \"Activity\": \"Work Block 1\",\n  \"Start Time\": \"9:00\",\n  \"Duration (min)\": 120\n}\n\nIMPORTANT CALENDAR EVENTS:\n\nTreat all calendar events as important EXCEPT events whose summary contains:\n\n- test\n- testing\n- dummy\n- placeholder\n- debug\n- temporary\n\nIf uncertain, treat the event as important.\n\nCONFLICT DETECTION:\n\nFor every NEW calendar event:\n\n1. Extract its start time from start.dateTime.\n2. Extract its end time from end.dateTime.\n3. Convert the calendar times into minutes from midnight.\n4. Convert each routine Start Time into minutes from midnight.\n5. Calculate routine end time:\n\nroutine_end = routine_start + Duration (min)\n\nA conflict exists when:\n\nroutine_start < event_end\nAND\nroutine_end > event_start\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n- Calendar events are FIXED.\n- Do NOT move routines.\n- Do NOT shift routines.\n- Do NOT calculate replacement times.\n- Do NOT perform cascade scheduling.\n- Do NOT modify the routine.\n- Do NOT return the complete routine.\n- Do NOT return events that have no conflict.\n- Do NOT return events already present in DataState.\n- Use the original routine row_number.\n- Never return null as row_number.\n- If one routine conflicts with multiple NEW calendar events, return one conflict object for each event.\n- If one calendar event conflicts with multiple routines, return one conflict object for each conflicting routine.\n\nOUTPUT:\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nUse exactly this structure:\n\n{\n  \"conflicts\": [\n    {\n      \"row\": 6,\n      \"event_id\": \"example-id\",\n      \"event\": \"Daily Standup\",\n      \"event_start\": \"10:15\",\n      \"event_end\": \"11:00\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIf there are no NEW conflicts:\n\n{\n  \"conflicts\": []\n}\n\nDo not return markdown.\nDo not return code fences.\nDo not return explanations.\nDo not return any other fields.",
        "batching": {},
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.9
    },
